#
# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the differential fuzzer.
#
# Read this before trusting it. Suppressions are how leak checking gets
# quietly turned off, so each line here has to earn its place.
#
# The differential fuzzer embeds a CPython interpreter, because comparing
# against tiktoken in the same process is what makes ten million comparisons
# affordable. That interpreter is never finalised at exit, and the tiktoken
# extension never frees its rank tables, so every run reports several
# megabytes of leaks that belong to the reference implementation.
#
# That this is the reference and not Knap was established by experiment, not
# by reading the stack traces:
#
#   * Knap driven over the same generated inputs with no interpreter in the
#     process reports no leaks and no errors at all. That is
#     tests/fuzz/asan_solo.mojo, and it runs with no suppression file.
#   * Three lines of Mojo that import tiktoken and touch nothing else
#     reproduce all four leaks at byte identical sizes: 8651344, 5242896,
#     2406144 and 207552 bytes. No Knap code runs in that program.
#
# The second experiment is the one that matters. The sizes match exactly, so
# these allocations are not merely similar to the reported ones, they are the
# reported ones.
#
# The honest cost of this file: a genuine Knap leak whose allocation sits
# underneath a suppressed frame would be hidden. That is why asan_solo.mojo
# exists and why it is a separate continuous integration job. The
# unsuppressed run is what proves Knap does not leak; this run proves parity
# still holds while the sanitizer watches for memory errors.
#
# Deliberately narrow. Matching is by module, not by a wildcard, and there is
# no entry for the Mojo runtime or for anything Knap allocates.

# tiktoken's Rust extension: the merge rank hash tables and the vectors built
# from their keys, held for the process lifetime and never dropped.
leak:_tiktoken.cpython

# CPython itself: interned strings, the small object arenas, and the
# interpreter state. Not freed because the embedded interpreter is not
# finalised before the process exits.
leak:libpython3.12.so
